      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e !mem_relinquish_available simply means that reliniquish hypercall is not advertised for this VM and is not needed\n\nOk, maybe I missed that these pkvm_virtio_balloon_hyp_ops are registered by both protected and non-protected VMs (and thus, !mem_relinquish_available is the case for non-protected VMs, so in this case we do want the balloon driver to successfully initialize and we do want pkvm_page_relinquish() to silently do nothing). If that\u0027s the case, then yeah, my patch is indeed very wrong.\n\nSo just to confirm: are these pkvm_virtio_balloon_hyp_ops actually registered for npVMs? I see it is guarded at least by !kvm_arm_hyp_service_available(ARM_SMCCC_KVM_FUNC_HYP_MEMINFO) at the beginning of pkvm_init_hyp_services(), so, is ARM_SMCCC_KVM_FUNC_HYP_MEMINFO advertised to both pVMs and npVMs? From a brief look into pKVM code it seems like it is advertised to pVMs only (in kvm_handle_pvm_hvc64())?\n\n\u003e For your purpose, placing the WARN_ON() around the entire original predicate would be fine.\n\nOk, if you are saying it\u0027s ok to just move printing the warning from the balloon driver to here (without adjusting any logic), I can do that. (After all, my actual motivation is just to avoid printing the warning on x86.)",
